WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.564 --> 00:00:10.527
Discovery turns a rough idea into a product brief or a PRD. An analyst interviews you one question at a time, and you decide what goes into the document.

2
00:00:11.229 --> 00:00:18.610
Open Discovery in the sidebar and click New discovery. Give it a title, a starting idea, and the project it is for.

3
00:00:22.164 --> 00:00:31.956
How should the analyst work? As a Facilitator it only asks. As a Partner it also brings its own ideas, labelled as its own. Or choose Ideate for me.

4
00:00:32.656 --> 00:00:44.283
If your organization has a CEO, you can work with the CEO. It proposes an answer to each question, or prepares all the answers first for you to review. You always have the last word.

5
00:00:44.982 --> 00:00:50.806
A time limit works like a meeting, and a cost limit stops the session when it is used up. Click Start.

6
00:00:51.507 --> 00:00:58.184
The analyst asks the first question. Pick a quick answer, or write your own words, skip it, or park it for later.

7
00:00:58.884 --> 00:01:09.999
The phases run from Frame through Diverge, Converge and Stress test to Capture. The panel on the right collects ideas, assumptions, open questions and decisions as you go.

8
00:01:10.697 --> 00:01:19.550
Sometimes the analyst makes a proposal. Nothing changes until you choose Apply. Reject drops it, and Redirect sends your own words back.

9
00:01:20.255 --> 00:01:26.890
In Capture the analyst writes the PRD from the panel. Validate against the checklist shows what is still missing.

10
00:01:30.681 --> 00:01:37.870
Approve it, then Hand to BA. The business analyst gets an intake linked to the PRD and drafts the cards from it.

11
00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:43.285
You can pause a discovery at any time and come back the next day. Nothing is lost.
